bug_fix_claims |bug_id, state, session_id, claimed_at, heartbeat_at, prev_status, note|
    interpreter_class_identity_no_scope_fallback_fail_open_2026_11_27, fixing, p3sweep4-20261127, 2026-11-27T19:34:39Z, 2026-11-27T19:34:39Z, open, "wave9"

    interpreter_class_identity_no_scope_fallback_fail_open_2026_11_27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4-61127: reproduced (fixtures qd/qe each declaring class Gizmo; driver pattern-matches case Gizmo { n } with no Gizmo imported: before d=3 e=4 fail-open - both owners matched a name the entry never imported; positive control with an import correct). Root cause: src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/module_cache.rs:2196 class_identity_matches no-scope arm None => source == type_name - an owner-exact instance (__spl_flat_<owner>__Gizmo) was accepted by bare source name when the scope walk had no answer. Fix: None => !class_name_is_shared(type_name) && source == type_name - a shared name with no scope binding fails closed (owner decision 2026-11-27: classes are identified by owner module); a unique owner still resolves through the flat table. Spec test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_no_scope_fallback_spec.spl (SIMPLE_BIN convention) RED 1-fail on unpatched, GREEN 3/3 on the patched scratch (built from the final combined tree - a concurrent agent's module_cache hunk at ~2260 runtime_imported_class is NOT mine, left in place, combined state compiles clean); siblings same_name_class_body_identity 7/7, owner_identity 5/5, mixed_lane 1/1 GREEN. Harness note documented: SIMPLE_BIN must be repo-relative (the runner canonicalizes SIMPLE_BINARY to an absolute path the Windows spawn layer mangles). Residuals: the pure-Simple lane has a conceptually permissive arm at 10.frontend/core/interpreter/eval.spl:209 but its HIR resolves pattern names per module and rejects unbound ones - left untouched (no self-hosted binary to verify); the JIT lane same-name owner gap is the separately recorded jit_pattern_same_name_class_identity_unchecked_2026_11_27 (the spec asserts the interpreter lane only); same_name_class_owner_module_spec fails on both seeds with a pre-existing circular-import error unrelated to this change. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_no_scope_fallback_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_body_identity_spec.spl"
    interpreter_class_identity_no_scope_fallback_fail_open_2026_11_27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: reproduced (no-import driver matched BOTH owners' Gizmo by bare name: d=3 e=4). Root cause: module_cache.rs:2196 None => source == type_name accepted an owner-exact instance by bare source name when the scope walk had no answer. Fix: None => !class_name_is_shared(type_name) && source == type_name (shared name + no scope binding fails closed per owner decision 2026-11-27; unique owner still resolves via the flat table). Spec same_name_class_no_scope_fallback RED 1-fail to GREEN 3/3 on the patched scratch (built from the combined tree with a concurrent agent's module_cache hunk left in place); siblings body_identity 7/7, owner_identity 5/5, mixed_lane 1/1. Residuals: JIT same-name owner gap is the separately recorded jit_pattern_same_name_class_identity_unchecked_2026_11_27; pure-Simple lane rejected-name handling verified by design (no self-hosted binary to run). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_no_scope_fallback_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_body_identity_spec.spl"
